@startuml
!theme plain
title Catalog 1 of 3 · Public reads and role-based projection
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Visitor or customer" as U
actor "Manager" as MG
participant "Frontend" as F
participant "NestJS API" as A
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Listings ==
U -> F : Opens the store
F -> A : GET /categories
A -> DB : Categories
A --> F : 200
F -> A : GET /products?filters and pagination
note right of F : Without Authorization the route responds the same,\nbut not with the same content
A -> DB : Active products
A --> F : 200 PaginatedProducts

== The detail, and the trap ==
F -> A : GET /products/ID
activate A
alt Doesn't exist or is disabled for the caller
  A --> F : 404 NotFound
else Visible
  alt Caller is a manager
    A --> F : 200 ManagerProduct **with stock**
  else Public or customer
    A --> F : 200 Product **without stock**
  end
end
deactivate A
note over A, DB #ffe0e0
  The contract declares the two shapes with **anyOf**, and anyOf
  validates if **any** branch validates. A manager response missing
  a field falls through the public branch, and a customer response
  that includes stock also passes. The contract can't detect it in
  either direction: that's why the tests assert the **exact** set
  of keys, not the absence of three fields.
end note

MG -> F : Opens the panel
F -> A : GET /products\nAuthorization: manager Bearer
A --> F : 200 with stock and disabled products

@enduml
